    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0580" n="532" xml:id="pg532"/>

                <head>No. 310.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Andrews to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>7 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rue L’Evéché</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1876-12-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 6, 1876</date>. (Received
                        December 26.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 368, I now beg,
                    informally (for being absent from my post on leave, I am in doubt whether I
                    should number this communication), to hand you herewith the answers which I have
                    to-day received from the department of ecclesiastical affairs and public
                    instruction of Norway to questions which I submitted on the civil service.</p>
                <p>I have carefully read the answers, and they seem to me to contain interesting and
                    valuable information. The Norwegian Government is certainly entitled to many
                    thanks for being at the pains to furnish the answers in English.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>C. C. ANDREWS.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d310-a1.xml" xpointer="d310-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
